{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":19,"code":"PSA","name":"Psalms","testament":"OT"},"chapter":77,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"d","content":["To the chief Musician, to Jeduthun, A Psalm of Asaph. "]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"PSA 77:1"},"I cried unto God with my voice, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["even"]}," unto God with my voice; and he gave ear unto me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:1"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"PSA 77:2"},"In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord: my sore ran in the night, and ceased not: my soul refused to be comforted. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:2"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"PSA 77:3"},"I remembered God, and was troubled: I complained, and my spirit was overwhelmed. Selah. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:3"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"PSA 77:4"},"Thou holdest mine eyes waking: I am so troubled that I cannot speak. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:4"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"PSA 77:5"},"I have considered the days of old, the years of ancient times. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:5"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"PSA 77:6"},"I call to remembrance my song in the night: I commune with mine own heart: and my spirit made diligent search. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:6"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"PSA 77:7"},"Will the Lord cast off for ever? and will he be favourable no more? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:7"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"PSA 77:8"},"Is his mercy clean gone for ever? doth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["his"]}," promise fail for evermore? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:8"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"PSA 77:9"},"Hath God forgotten to be gracious? hath he in anger shut up his tender mercies? Selah. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:9"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"PSA 77:10"},"And I said, This ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," my infirmity: ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["but I will remember "]},"the years of the right hand of the most High. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:10"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"PSA 77:11"},"I will remember the works of the LORD: surely I will remember thy wonders of old. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:11"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"PSA 77:12"},"I will meditate also of all thy work, and talk of thy doings. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:12"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"PSA 77:13"},"Thy way, O God, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," in the sanctuary: who ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is so "]},"great a God as ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["our"]}," God? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:13"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"PSA 77:14"},"Thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["art"]}," the God that doest wonders: thou hast declared thy strength among the people. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:14"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"PSA 77:15"},"Thou hast with ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["thine"]}," arm redeemed thy people, the sons of Jacob and Joseph. Selah. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:15"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"PSA 77:16"},"The waters saw thee, O God, the waters saw thee; they were afraid: the depths also were troubled. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:16"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"PSA 77:17"},"The clouds poured out water: the skies sent out a sound: thine arrows also went abroad. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:17"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"PSA 77:18"},"The voice of thy thunder ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["was"]}," in the heaven: the lightnings lightened the world: the earth trembled and shook. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:18"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"PSA 77:19"},"Thy way ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," in the sea, and thy path in the great waters, and thy footsteps are not known. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:19"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"PSA 77:20"},"Thou leddest thy people like a flock by the hand of Moses and Aaron. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 77:20"}]}]}
